<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-RESULTS FROM LEOPARDSTOWN.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-RESULTS FROM LEOPARDSTOWN.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of major races at</p>
<p>Leopardstown on Saturday:</p>
<p>William Neville and Sons Novice Chase run over three miles</p>
<p>(4.8-km)</p>
<p>1. Dorans Pride (5-1 on favourite) ridden by Shane Broderick</p>
<p>2. Le Ginno (9-2) Tommy Treacy</p>
<p>3. Garabagh (25-1) Paul Carberry</p>
<p>Four ran: Winner owned by Tom Doran and trained by Michael</p>
<p>Hourigan in Ireland.</p>
<p>Distances: distance, distance (note: distance signifies at</p>
<p>least more than 30 lengths.)</p>
<p>Value to winner 6,850 Irish pounds ($11,400)  </p>
<p>Ericsson Chase run over three miles (4.8-km).</p>
<p>1. Johnny Setaside (2-1 favourite) Richard Dunwoody</p>
<p>2. King of the Gales (16-1) Francis Woods</p>
<p>3. Opera Hat (7-2) Anthony Powell</p>
<p>Seven ran: Winner owned by John O'Meara and trained by Noel</p>
<p>Meade in Ireland.</p>
<p>Distances: three lengths, 15 lengths.  </p>
<p>Value to  winner of 32,500 Irish pounds ($45,000).</p>
</text>
